\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Benchmark comparison on \texttt  {uifo\_800\_3000} (1 logical CPU). (a)~On AMD EPYC 9334 (\texttt  {results/amd-epyc/}), median warm execution drops from 16.952\,s to 0.0969\,s ($174.9\times $ speedup). (b)~First-run end-to-end on EPYC 9334 drops from 35.829\,s to 0.895--0.964\,s ($37.2$--$40.0\times $ speedup). (c)~On i7-1355U WSL2, \texttt  {final/combined-v2} (\texttt  {benchmark-v2.json}) cuts first-run end-to-end from 3.97\,s to 3.18\,s ($-20\%$) and XLA compile from 1.52\,s to 0.87\,s ($-43\%$) vs.\ \texttt  {final/combined}. Best viewed in color.}}{7}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:benchmarks}{{4}{7}{Benchmark comparison on \texttt {uifo\_800\_3000} (1 logical CPU). (a)~On AMD EPYC 9334 (\texttt {results/amd-epyc/}), median warm execution drops from 16.952\,s to 0.0969\,s ($174.9\times $ speedup). (b)~First-run end-to-end on EPYC 9334 drops from 35.829\,s to 0.895--0.964\,s ($37.2$--$40.0\times $ speedup). (c)~On i7-1355U WSL2, \texttt {final/combined-v2} (\texttt {benchmark-v2.json}) cuts first-run end-to-end from 3.97\,s to 3.18\,s ($-20\%$) and XLA compile from 1.52\,s to 0.87\,s ($-43\%$) vs.\ \texttt {final/combined}. Best viewed in color}{figure.4}{}}
